<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://btx-community.com/">
  <title>[Draft] Design drafts · BTX Community</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Layout drafts for btx-community.com, for feedback. Not the official site.">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:title" content="[Draft] Design drafts for btx-community.com – not the official layout">
  <meta property="og:description" content="Layout drafts for btx-community.com, for feedback. Not the official site.">
  <link rel="icon" href="{{ icon_url }}" type="image/svg+xml">
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="48x48">
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ touch_icon_url }}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ overview_css }}">
</head>
<body class="drafts">
  <a class="drafts__skip" href="#main">{{ ui["skip"] }}</a>
  <div class="draft-banner" role="note">
    <p class="draft-banner__text"><strong>Design drafts</strong> – not the official layout. Content may lag behind.
      <a class="draft-banner__link" href="{{ feedback }}" rel="noopener noreferrer">Feedback ↗</a></p>
  </div>
  <main class="drafts__main" id="main">
    <h1 class="drafts__title">Design drafts for btx-community.com</h1>
    <p class="drafts__lead">Layouts to compare on real content before anything is decided. They read the same content files as the live site, in English only, and none of them replaces it. The official site stays at <a href="/">btx-community.com →</a></p>
    <ul class="drafts__list">
      {%- for name, design, href in designs %}
      <li class="drafts__item">
        <a class="drafts__card" href="{{ href }}">
          <span class="drafts__name">{{ design.title }}</span>
          <span class="drafts__summary">{{ design.summary }}</span>
          <span class="drafts__open">Open the draft <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
        </a>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <h2 class="drafts__h2">Tell us what you think</h2>
    <p>One issue collects the feedback on all drafts, with three questions: what is faster than on the live site, what is missing, and what is worse than before.</p>
    <p><a href="{{ feedback }}" rel="noopener noreferrer">Feedback issue on GitHub ↗</a></p>
    <p class="drafts__arrows">→ goes to a page of this site · ↗ opens another site</p>
  </main>
  <footer class="drafts__foot">
    <p>{{ ui["disclaimer"] }}</p>
    <p><a href="{{ repo_url }}" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ ui["repo"] }} ↗</a> · {{ version }}</p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
